⬇️FULL RECIPE⬇️
281 calories 37g protein (for the entire pint, mix-ins/toppings included)

Frosted Sugar Cookie Protein Blizzard 😋🍦

Original recipe from my Recipe Book

Check out the link in my bio for my Creami Recipe Book with over 150 recipes like this one!

- 400g Fat Free High Protein Milk
- 35g Monk Fruit sweetener
- 5g (1 tsp) vanilla bean paste (or extract)
- A pinch of salt
- 1g (¼ tsp) xanthan gum
Mix-ins/toppings:
- 15g protein frosting (can sub with normal frosting)
• Mix 15g of your favorite protein powder with a splash of water (add water very slowly and mix until it becomes a frosting-like consistency)
- ⅓ of a package of the Fuul Birthday Cake Cookie Dough bites
- (Optional) ½ tsp Christmas-themed sprinkles
281 cal 24g C, 4g F, 37g P

Instructions:
1. Blend all ingredients for the base and freeze (at least 16 hours)
2. Prep the protein frosting
• In a cup, slowly add water to 15g of protein powder. Stir until it reaches a frosting-like consistency. Refrigerate until you’re ready to use it.
3. Run your pint under hot water for at least 60 seconds
4. Spin on “Lite Ice Cream” setting
5. Respin if very powdery
6. Make a hole down to the bottom with a butter knife and fill with the frosting
7. Run the “Mix-in” cycle
8. Top with the cookie dough bites and sprinkles

